  "A_lambda_fields_status": "ORIENTATION-BUG SUPERSEDED. The A1_matrix_bits/A2_matrix_bits/fredholm_lambda_bits fields recorded in koubou83_survival_v3_20260822.json for the order2 representatives are NOT trusted and NOT reproduced in this cert. Per commander instruction (2026-08-22), repair of the A1/A2 construction is DEFERRED until the mathematician delivers an unambiguous redefinition of the boxed-formula operator orientation; no repair has been attempted here. The linear-algebra (A1/A2) system remains NEEDED for future depth-K DIES verdicts (a witness-search/Phi-only check alone cannot produce a definitive DIES certificate) and will be rebuilt once the orientation is pinned down, then re-cross-checked against the cross-checker's own A1/A2 for agreement.",
  "claim_boundary": "Verdicts are ONLY about lifting to depth K=[N,N]N^2 (the mod-2 relative Frattini refinement of N=N_PB3). SURVIVES-K does NOT imply genuine/arithmetic realizability -- it means the hexagon conditions (3.3)/(3.4) can be satisfied one step deeper than N for SOME correction w in N (here: w=identity for both order3 representatives, and an explicit nontrivial witness sigma-word of length 308 (window 154161) / 248 (window 154163) for both order2 representatives). m is FIXED at 0 throughout (R-b design scope). Grade: candidate / cross-checked (two independent systems: producer's corrected witness-based recheck + cross-checker's own build) -- 'verified' remains reserved for Lean, not used here.",
